<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Our story</h2>
    <p>
      Precious Steps was established in {{ site.foundedYear }}, licensed for
      fifteen children. In 2000 we were awarded an early childhood contract
      through Plainfield Public Schools, which allowed us to offer early
      childhood education to resident children and families, and we moved to a
      larger facility licensed for forty-five children.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our reputation for caring for infants and toddlers grew our waiting list
      beyond what one building could hold, so we opened a second location
      dedicated to infants and toddlers. At the same time we began pursuing
      accreditation through the National Association for the Education of Young
      Children. It was an arduous process, and we have been accredited since
      2006.
    </p>
    <p>
      In 2007 we acquired the facility and contracted classrooms of a child care
      program that was closing, increasing our Pre-K enrollment to 120. In 2013
      we accepted an invitation to participate in Grow NJ Kids, the state
      quality rating initiative, which put every policy and procedure under
      review. That work earned us 4 of 5 stars at Arlington Avenue and 3 of 5
      stars at Washington Avenue.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--subtle">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>Our educational philosophy</h2>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        From birth, a baby's brain cells multiply wildly, making connections
        that may shape a lifetime of experience. The first five years are
        critical.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      That idea is the cornerstone of our philosophy. Growth and development do
      not happen by chance. They are achieved through planned and spontaneous
      interactive learning experiences that stimulate the senses and foster
      development physically, cognitively, socially, emotionally, and
      creatively.
    </p>
    <p>
      In partnership with our parents, we provide a warm and nurturing setting
      reminiscent of a child's most natural environment, home. There are
      opportunities for solitary play as well as group activities, and our staff
      serve as positive role models offering care that is supportive and
      responsive to each child's individual needs.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <h2>An anti-bias community</h2>
    <p>
      We work to promote and create an inclusive environment that encourages
      conversations among children and adults about difference, without
      judgement. It is our goal that all of our children and their families feel
      respected, included, and reflected in our early childhood classrooms.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

