    <p>
      Our director began her career in early childhood education in 1984 at a
      Head Start program in Jersey City, having just earned a BA in Psychology
      with a concentration in Child Development and a minor in Business
      Management.
    </p>
    <p>
      Her work with children facing developmental challenges carried her through
      early intervention programs in New York and New Jersey, a rehabilitative
      program in Atlanta serving medically fragile children, and finally the
      role of New Jersey Central Regional Special Needs Coordinator, before she
      became the owner and operator of Precious Steps.
    </p>
    <p>
      That experience shapes the center to this day. Precious Steps consistently
      welcomes children with special challenges and ensures that they and their
      families feel supported. Families are frequently referred to us by the
      district for exactly that reason.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

